  "title": "Review Bombed",
  "subtitle": "\"His name was on 47 one-star reviews of my novel. My publisher said the fix was to date him publicly.\"",
  "penName": "Ada Sinclair",
  "genre": "fakeDating",
  "hook": "My debut novel got forty-seven one-star reviews in a single afternoon. The pattern was surgical. All posted by different accounts — all coming from the same IP in Brooklyn — all quoting Callum Brennan, the litfic bro whose novel I had once called *performatively masculine* on a podcast he'd never heard. My publisher called. Her solution was a joint book tour, a public rivalry-turned-romance, and a fake relationship. Callum's publisher was demanding the same. We were introduced in a conference room in midtown. He walked in, read my opening line aloud, and said *I did not write those reviews.*",
